{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel journeyed.</b> Even though they saw that the prayer of the righteous shields his generation and that it is fitting to lament over his death, some of them — or the majority — who were pasturing flocks in the wilderness journeyed to Moserah to find water and pasture for the sheep. While they were there Aaron died and was buried, and Elazar ministered as priest. They did not come to lament over the death or to mourn at the burial, nor did they take care to honor Elazar who ministered in his stead — but from there they journeyed to Gudgodah to pasture the sheep." "<b>And from Gudgodah, Jotbathah, a land of brooks of water.</b> For all those places now mentioned were a land of streams suited for pasturing sheep, and they did not set their heart to be distressed over the harm caused by the death of the righteous, nor to his honor or the honor of his son."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:03.480572600Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}